From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a7s: arm WDT_CPUS instead of WDT0

sunxi-cubie-a7s-watchdog-autostart turned on WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART, and U-Boot arms every watchdog
it probes: initr_watchdog() walks the whole WDT uclass and starts each
device with autostart set, registering each for sysreset as well
(drivers/watchdog/wdt-uclass.c). On this board that was WDT0
(watchdog@2050000 in sun60i-a733.dtsi).

WDT0 does not reset this board reliably. On the test board it reset a halted panic
(panic=0) in 7 of 13 runs and a hard hang of all eight CPUs in 1 of 2.
WDT_CPUS, the watchdog in the CPUS domain, armed from Linux with busybox
devmem, reset 3 of 3 of those panics pinned to CPU2 and one unfed timeout;
BL31's PSCI SYSTEM_RESET already resets through its SRST register (measured
2026-09-15). The kernel DT moves to WDT_CPUS (kernel patch
arm64-dts-a733-cubie-a7s-watchdog-on-wdt-cpus), the way
upstream disables the H6's main watchdog ("Broken on some H6 boards").

The change:

  * A7S board DT: &wdt status = "disabled" -- U-Boot no longer binds,
    starts or registers WDT0.
  * A7S board DT: r_watchdog: watchdog@7021000 under /soc. A733 UM 8.3.5
    lists WDT_CPUS at 0x07021000 with the same registers as WDT0; UM
    Table 12-1 INTID 223 "S_WDT" gives GIC SPI 191. compatible is the WDT0
    node's; the driver matches sun55i-a523-wdt (CTRL 0x0c, CFG 0x10, MODE
    0x14, as UM 8.3.6). sunxi_wdt_probe() maps the register base, stops the
    timer and takes no clock. The clocks copy radxa's WDT0 node, hosc =
    <&osc24M> included -- the A523 value the kernel patch
    arm64-dts-a733-feed-the-watchdog-hosc-from-the-dcxo replaces with the
    DCXO; nothing in U-Boot reads it.
  * CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y: `wdt dev watchdog@7021000` and `wdt stop` at the
    prompt. The image is designed as the only system on the board, whatever
    it boots from. A system that does not know WDT_CPUS is reset about 16 s
    after this U-Boot boots it -- the vendor system on the eMMC of one test
    board knows only WDT0 -- and stopping the watchdog at the prompt is how
    such a system is reached.

One difference from the UM that this patch does not change:
sun60i-a733.dtsi gives WDT0 GIC SPI 63, the A523's value; the A733's WDT0
is SPI 106 (UM Table 12-1). U-Boot's watchdog driver uses no interrupt and
the node is disabled here, so it is left as radxa has it.

Pairing, in both directions: with the autostart alone U-Boot hands an armed
WDT0 to a kernel that has moved to WDT_CPUS, which neither stops nor feeds
it; with this patch U-Boot hands an armed WDT_CPUS to a kernel that still
uses WDT0, which does not feed it. Kernel and boot chain come from one build
of this repository.

Timeout and feeding are unchanged from the autostart (16 s, the uclass's
cyclic reset). Linux keeps a watchdog it finds running (sunxi_wdt since
v6.18.53).

Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/src/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/src/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -273,3 +273,27 @@
 	pcie1v8-supply = <&reg_bldo1>;
 	pcie3v3-supply = <&reg_dcdc1>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * The watchdog U-Boot arms (WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART) and the one Linux
+ * feeds from here on is WDT_CPUS. WDT0 is disabled: on the test board it reset a halted
+ * panic 7 of 13 times and a hard hang of all CPUs 1 of 2; WDT_CPUS reset 3 of 3
+ * of those panics on CPU2 and its own unfed timeout (measured 2026-09-15). The
+ * kernel DT does the same, the way upstream disables the H6's main
+ * watchdog.
+ */
+&wdt {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&{/soc} {
+	/* UM 8.3.5 WDT_CPUS @ 0x07021000; UM Table 12-1 INTID 223 -> GIC SPI 191. */
+	r_watchdog: watchdog@7021000 {
+		compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-wdt",
+			     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-wdt";
+		reg = <0x7021000 0x20>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 191 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		clocks = <&osc24M>, <&rtc CLK_OSC32K>;
+		clock-names = "hosc", "losc";
+	};
+};
--- a/src/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
+++ b/src/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@ CONFIG_WDT=y
 CONFIG_WDT_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART=y
+CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3
 CONFIG_SYS_BOOTCOUNT_ADDR=0x0709011C
